{"seq":12,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-none-mu-v02-heldout/ms-06-phl-tickets/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T05:27:11.639Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"1dd164dc5c7592cbfac083d25bb2a577e00104d8680268b915a6e88247af57f1","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, here's the list for Kwame's review. I checked #coastal-team, #coastal-random, Moss's four Coastal digests and your Pellucid cutover note. Pellow Home Living and Covey & Lark Retail are left out, along with Saltmarsh.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL, Gulf Coast)**\n- **#4419, open:** The `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. This is from Moss's Coastal cheat sheet.\n- **PD-8841:** Pemberline Dock handles chassis pool holds badly on double-booked gates (Gate 4B), and Hector, the night dispatcher, raised it. This is from your 8 Dec cutover note.\n- **Berth 2 yard map CSV import bug:** The same note mentions it, but it gives no ticket number.\n- **Chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change:** The cheat sheet calls this the main friction point and gives no ticket number.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF, Puget Sound)**\n- **Feature request #882:** Warehouse managers want a bulk-clear button for departed barges. This is from the cheat sheet.\n- **Tide-table import macro failure on Terminal B:** Engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch. The cheat sheet gives no ticket number.\n- **Patched manifest CSV:** DMF asked for this before the 06:00 shift, per Moss's 2 Nov digest. It has no ticket number and is probably the same issue as the Terminal B failure, though the notes don't say so.\n\n**Check before the review**\n- **#4419 is contradictory.** The cheat sheet puts it on PHL as the Yard_Dwell_Summary timeout. Moss's 2 Nov digest lists it under \"Puget Sound Operations\" as a barge slip 7 schedule sync issue, in the same bullet as the DMF manifest request. Kwame should confirm which account it belongs to.\n- **#882 is not #8812.** #8812 is the Door 4B scanner ticket on the Pellow account, which I excluded.\n- **There may be more tickets.** I couldn't see any ticket files under the account folders, so this covers only what's in the channels and notes."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
